<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llantwit Major</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Llanilltud Fawr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Llantwit Major is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vale-of-glamorgan">Vale of Glamorgan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, whose Welsh name, Llanilltud Fawr, recalls the monastery founded there by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illtud">Saint Illtud</a> around 500. It was one of the great centres of learning of early Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and its church holds a collection of early medieval inscribed crosses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llantwit-major.jpg" alt="Llantwit Major" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glyn Baker · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llantwit_Major,_East_Street.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
